>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `MODEL_REFUTE_TAC`

``` hol4
Refute.MODEL_REFUTE_TAC : tactic
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Searches for a counterexample with the finite model finder.

`MODEL_REFUTE_TAC` is `REFUTE_TAC_WITH [upd_search (Only [ModelFinder])]`,
which runs the `kodkod` backend.  It needs the external Kodkodi
component; without it the outcome is `Unknown`.  With the `falsify`
field false it searches for a model of the goal instead.

### Failure

Fails only if the configuration's `expect` field is not met.

### Comments

The model finder leaves unconstrained the `ARB` case HOL4 adds to a
non-exhaustive definition, so a goal true only because of that case
can get a counterexample, as in Isabelle's Nitpick.

